//
// CDtapiLite - Every I/O configuration code, in numeric order, as an X-macro list
//
// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
//
// Each entry is X(Name, Kinds, Parent1, Parent2):
//
//   Name     the DTAPI_IOCONFIG_ macro name without its prefix. The name string and the
//            numeric code of an entry both expand from this one token, so they cannot
//            disagree.
//   Kinds    what the code can be in a configuration, as DTL_IOCFG_ flags: a group, a
//            boolean I/O capability (which is configured like a group), a value, a
//            sub-value. A code can be more than one.
//   Parents  the codes this one may appear under: the group of a value, the value of a
//            sub-value. DTL_IOCFG_NONE fills an unused slot, and DTL_IOCFG_ANY_BOOLIO
//            stands for every boolean I/O capability, which is where TRUE and FALSE
//            belong.
//
// Including this file with X defined expands the list:
//
//     #define X(Name, Kinds, Parent1, Parent2) { #Name, DTAPI_IOCONFIG_##Name },
//     #include "Tables/DtlIoConfigList.inc"
//     #undef X
//
// The order is numeric so that the table can be indexed by code. A unit test checks
// that every code from zero upwards appears exactly once, so a new constant added to
// CDtapiLite.h without an entry here fails that test rather than going unnoticed.
//
// The kinds and parents are what DTAPI validates a configuration against. They are
// derived from DekTec's capability definitions by Scripts/extract_ioconfig_relation.py,
// which repeats the derivation of DekTec's CapParser; see
// Documentation/0003-device-layer.md.
//
// No include guard: the file is meant to be included more than once.

